WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.990 align:start position:0%
 
[Music]  one of america's busiest airports is  back in business  after a serious security breach and a  wild police chase across two runways  authorities want to know exactly how one  car got through a  fence on the perimeter of lax there it  is jonathan vigliotti reports  this was the scene as the driver in a  silver mazda  led police on a high-speed chase across  one of the highest trafficked areas in  the country  the tarmac at los angeles international  airport huge ripple effect here after a  vehicle actually breached the airport  facilities after breaking through a  fence near the airport's fedex cargo  facility  the driver sped past a line of parked  jumbo jets  witnesses then say the car drove across  two busy runways on the airport's south  side  did a u-turn back across them before  coming to a halt  outside a private terminal the large  chain-link gate near the fedex loading  area was found  completely destroyed police gave chase  most of the time until the hatchback  stopped outside atlantic aviation  a charterjet terminal this is a really  crazy one more than a dozen police cars  surrounded the vehicle  and the driver surrendered when the car  came to arrest  the letters inexplicably for now s.o.s  were clearly visible on the hood police  have not released the identity of the  driver or what the motive may have been  nobody was injured during this chase but  the question remains  how a major breach like this could have  happened in the first place  jonathan cbs news los angeles

